# 0013. Claude Code in the editor: claudecode.nvim next to Copilot

- Status: Accepted
- Date: 2026-11-11

Claude Code connects to Neovim through `coder/claudecode.nvim` for chat, code generation
and reviewed diffs; Copilot stays for inline hints as you type. All AI keys sit under
`\a`.

## Technical details
- **Problem**: Claude Code ran in a tmux pane with no link to nvim. It couldn't see the
  open file or selection, its edits landed on disk unreviewed, and there were no keys for
  AI at all except `<Tab>` (accept Copilot).
- **Plugin** (`lua/plugins/coding.lua`): `coder/claudecode.nvim`, the same IDE protocol
  the VS Code extension uses (a websocket server plus a lock file in `~/.claude/ide/`).
  Lazy-loaded on its commands and keys, so startup doesn't change; the server starts when
  the plugin loads. Terminal: snacks split on the right (snacks is already installed).
  A `claude` already running in a tmux pane can attach to the same server with `/ide`.
  `focus_after_send = true`: after sending code you type the request straight away.
- **Keys** (`\a` = "ai" in which-key; `\A` stays "adr"):
  - `\ac` toggle Claude, `\af` focus it, `\ar` resume a session, `\am` pick model.
  - `\ab` add the current buffer as context; `\as` (visual) send the selection: this is
    code generation (select, send, say "write the tests" / "refactor this").
    In oil, `\as` adds the file under the cursor.
  - `\aa` / `\ad` accept / reject the diff Claude proposes.
  - `\ai` toggle Copilot inline hints on and off (`:Copilot enable/disable`).
  - Insert mode: `<M-]>` / `<M-[>` cycle Copilot suggestions (copilot.vim defaults).
    `<M-\>` (copilot's "suggest now") is taken by tmux (split right), so it's left alone.
- **Consequences**: one place for AI keys, edits show up as diffs you accept. Two AI
  tools stay installed: Claude has no ghost-text completion. The Claude terminal inside
  nvim and the tmux pane are two ways to do the same thing; pick per session.

## Technologies and alternatives
- Involved: claudecode.nvim, snacks.nvim terminal, copilot.vim, which-key.
- Alternatives: avante.nvim / codecompanion.nvim: their own chat UI calling the API with
  a key, no Claude Code tools, skills or CLAUDE.md. A Claude-backed completion source for
  blink (minuet-ai): paid API calls on every keystroke, and Copilot already does this.
